## Pillar 1 — The Evidence Machine
*"Every insight comes with a receipt."*

This is Nudgeio's philosophical moat. Every competitor shows charts and calls them insights. Nudgeio shows **the evidence chain behind every claim** — the specific commits, spec changes, PR comments, Slack threads, and CI failures that caused the pattern. This is not a feature — it is the architecture.

| # | Feature | Why It's Different / Unsolved |
|---|---------|-------------------------------|
| 1.1 | **Evidence-Backed Causal Timelines** — Any metric change (cycle time spike, DORA degradation, sprint slip) renders a step-by-step narrative: Trigger → Evidence → Chain of causation → Diagnosis. Every claim is a hyperlinked citation to the source artifact. | Allstacks, Faros, Swarmia, DX all claim "root cause" — none expose an explicit, navigable evidence chain the user can dispute or inspect. |
| 1.2 | **Competing Hypothesis Engine** — For every diagnosis, Nudgeio surfaces 3 ranked hypotheses with individual confidence scores and the evidence supporting (or contradicting) each. "Primary: review congestion — 84%. Secondary: late spec expansion — 61%. Weak: external dependency blockage — 38%." | No competitor models alternative hypotheses with confidence scores visible to users. All deliver one AI narrative. |
| 1.3 | **Outcome Validation Loop** — After a diagnosis is accepted and an action is taken, Nudgeio tracks whether the prediction proved correct. "Review congestion diagnosed → review ownership rebalanced → review wait fell 39% over 3 sprints → diagnosis confirmed." | No competitor closes the loop from diagnosis → intervention → outcome proof. The prediction is never verified. |
| 1.4 | **Evidence Drawer UI** — Any metric tile, any insight card, any causal claim is clickable into a provenance drawer: raw source artifact, extraction method, confidence level. "Show me the Slack message that triggered this." | Every competitor shows aggregated data points. None expose the underlying source with full provenance. |
| 1.5 | **Fact vs Inference Separation** — Observed facts (commit timestamps, merge events) are visually and architecturally separated from inferences (sentiment, intent, causation). Confidence scores are shown at inference level, not hidden inside a black-box model. | No competitor makes this separation explicit. AI conclusions are presented with the same certainty as raw metrics. |

